  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. A long session (WBS 8.5) of 52 inputs whose only fight, against two thugs, comes early, from input 5. Pell is not a spellcaster and has no way to heal, so the hit points lost at inputs 5 to 11 hold for the remaining 40 inputs: inputs 13, 45 and 51 invite a hit-point band phrase 2, 34 and 40 inputs after the fight. This is the longest gap in the suite between damage and its recall. The night's sleep at input 50 restores nothing (no rests). Two numeric threads: parcels go 3, 2, 1, 0 at inputs 2, 14, 28 and 40, and fish go 4, 2, 0 at inputs 19, 21 and 34; input 43 asks for what is left, which is the dagger and the lantern. Fish are traded and the lantern is gained as two separate changes, because items do not move between inventories. Input 44 spends coin, and there is no currency in the game. Three quests: the parcels run to stage 3 and complete, Marta's net completes at stage 2, and the mooring toll (max_stage 1) fails at input 33. Three NPCs and both directions: Marta goes up once to allied, the ferryman up to friendly at input 22 and back down to neutral at input 37, and the harbour master down from unfriendly to hostile at input 24 and back up to unfriendly at input 31. Input 48 asks the ferryman how he feels, after he went up and then down. Inputs 5 to 11 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
